Skill "formal-audit-phase1" completed (forked execution).

Result:
Based on my comprehensive analysis of the Prysm consensus layer codebase, I can now provide the Phase 1 Abstract Interpretation analysis for ether conservation across balance operations.

```json
{
  "phase1_abstract_interpretation": {
    "summary": "Analysis of ether conservation in Prysm consensus layer reveals that 'move_ether' is not a direct EVM operation but rather implemented through abstract balance manipulation primitives (IncreaseBalance/DecreaseBalance). The consensus layer maintains validator balances in an abstract state machine where balance transfers occur through state transitions rather than EVM ether transfers. Abstract interpretation identified multiple balance flow operations with conservation guarantees and overflow/underflow protections.",
    "state_anomalies_found": [
      {
        "anomaly_id": "AI-001",
        "type": "Not Applicable - Architectural Mismatch",
        "severity": "Informational",
        "location": "N/A - Consensus Layer Design",
        "description": "The term 'move_ether' does not exist as an operation in the Prysm consensus layer. This is a Consensus Layer (Beacon Chain) client, not an Execution Layer (EVM) client. Ether transfers in the consensus layer are abstracted as balance state transitions.",
        "abstract_domain_analysis": {
          "balance_representation": "uint64 (gwei units)",
          "domain_bounds": "[0, 2^64-1]",
          "state_machine": "Beacon State with validator balances array"
        }
      },
      {
        "anomaly_id": "AI-002",
        "type": "Balance Conservation Analysis",
        "severity": "Low",
        "location": "Multiple balance operation sites",
        "description": "Balance transfers in consensus layer follow a decrease-then-increase pattern. Conservation depends on correct pairing of operations.",
        "operations_analyzed": [
          {
            "operation": "IncreaseBalance",
            "file": "target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/helpers/rewards_penalties.go:104-114",
            "abstract_state": {
              "input_domain": "balances[idx] ∈ [0, 2^64-1], delta ∈ [0, 2^64-1]",
              "operation": "balances[idx] := balances[idx] + delta",
              "output_domain": "balances[idx] ∈ [0, 2^64-1] with overflow protection",
              "overflow_protection": "Uses math.Add64 which returns error on overflow (line 128)",
              "conservation_property": "Σ(all_balances) increases by exactly delta"
            }
          },
          {
            "operation": "DecreaseBalance",
            "file": "target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/helpers/rewards_penalties.go:140-146",
            "abstract_state": {
              "input_domain": "balances[idx] ∈ [0, 2^64-1], delta ∈ [0, 2^64-1]",
              "operation": "balances[idx] := max(0, balances[idx] - delta)",
              "output_domain": "balances[idx] ∈ [0, 2^64-1] with underflow protection",
              "underflow_protection": "Saturates at 0 if delta > currBalance (line 160-162)",
              "conservation_property": "Σ(all_balances) decreases by min(delta, balances[idx])"
            }
          },
          {
            "operation": "SlashValidator",
            "file": "target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/validators/validator.go:235-304",
            "abstract_state": {
              "balance_flow": "slashed_balance → proposer_balance + whistleblower_balance",
              "decrease_source": "DecreaseBalance(slashedIdx, slashingPenalty) at line 281",
              "increase_targets": [
                "IncreaseBalance(proposerIdx, proposerReward) at line 298",
                "IncreaseBalance(whistleBlowerIdx, whistleblowerReward - proposerReward) at line 301"
              ],
              "conservation_analysis": "Partial conservation: slashingPenalty is destroyed (burned), only whistleblowerReward is redistributed",
              "potential_loss": "slashingPenalty - whistleblowerReward is permanently removed from circulation"
            }
          },
          {
            "operation": "ProcessPendingConsolidations",
            "file": "target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/electra/consolidations.go:43-91",
            "abstract_state": {
              "balance_flow": "source_validator_balance → target_validator_balance",
              "amount": "min(balances[source], effective_balance[source])",
              "decrease_operation": "DecreaseBalance(sourceIndex, amount) at line 77",
              "increase_operation": "IncreaseBalance(targetIndex, amount) at line 80",
              "conservation_property": "Perfect conservation: Σ(balances) unchanged, amount transferred from source to target",
              "atomicity": "Both operations in same transaction; no intermediate state observable"
            }
          },
          {
            "operation": "ProcessWithdrawals",
            "file": "target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/blocks/withdrawals.go:154-227",
            "abstract_state": {
              "balance_flow": "validator_balance → execution_layer (external)",
              "operation": "DecreaseBalance(validatorIndex, withdrawalAmount) at line 192",
              "conservation_scope": "Breaks conservation within consensus layer by design - transfers to execution layer",
              "external_transfer": "Balance leaves consensus layer state machine"
            }
          },
          {
            "operation": "ProcessPendingDeposits",
            "file": "target_workspace/beacon-chain/core/electra/deposits.go:257-370",
            "abstract_state": {
              "balance_flow": "execution_layer (external) → validator_balance",
              "operation": "IncreaseBalance(validatorIndex, depositAmount) at lines 324, 338, 400",
              "conservation_scope": "Breaks conservation within consensus layer by design - receives from execution layer",
              "external_transfer": "Balance enters consensus layer state machine"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "anomaly_id": "AI-003",
        "type": "Overflow Protection Verification",
        "severity": "Low",
        "location": "target_workspace/math/math_helper.go",
        "description": "All balance increase operations use Add64 with overflow detection",
        "abstract_analysis": {
          "overflow_detection": "bits.Add64 with carry bit check (line 143-148)",
          "error_propagation": "Returns ErrAddOverflow on overflow",
          "impact": "Prevents uint64 wraparound that would violate conservation"
        }
      },
      {
        "anomaly_id": "AI-004",
        "type": "State Consistency - Asymmetric Conservation",
        "severity": "Medium",
        "location": "Multiple operations",
        "description": "Ether conservation varies by operation type: (1) Internal transfers perfectly conserve, (2) Slashing operations intentionally destroy ether, (3) Cross-layer operations (deposits/withdrawals) conserve at system level but not within consensus layer alone",
        "conservation_classes": {
          "perfect_conservation": [
            "ProcessPendingConsolidations (consolidations.go:77-80)",
            "Balance topups for existing validators (deposits.go:338)"
          ],
          "intentional_burn": [
            "SlashValidator penalties (validator.go:281) - slashingPenalty partially burned"
          ],
          "cross_layer_transfer": [
            "ProcessWithdrawals (withdrawals.go:192) - consensus to execution",
            "ProcessPendingDeposits (deposits.go:324) - execution to consensus"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "anomaly_id": "AI-005",
        "type": "Abstract Domain Completeness",
        "severity": "Informational",
        "location": "Global",
        "description": "The balance state space is well-defined with clear invariants",
        "invariants": {
          "type_invariant": "∀i. balances[i] ∈ [0, 2^64-1]",
          "overflow_safety": "∀increase_op. overflow → error (no wraparound)",
          "underflow_safety": "∀decrease_op. underflow → saturate_to_zero",
          "total_supply_bounded": "Σ(balances) ≤ num_validators × 2^64",
          "conservation_per_operation": {
            "internal_transfer": "Δ(Σ balances) = 0",
            "slashing": "Δ(Σ balances) < 0 (intentional burn)",
            "deposit": "Δ(Σ balances) > 0 (from execution layer)",
            "withdrawal": "Δ(Σ balances) < 0 (to execution layer)"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

